## 14. Success Criteria

The project shall be considered successful when:

1. The M18 proximity sensor can be installed correctly.
2. The sensor remains securely fixed during use.
3. The bracket can be mounted securely to an external structure.
4. The design can be manufactured successfully using FDM printing.
5. The assembly uses standard metric hardware.
6. The sensor can be removed and replaced without damaging the bracket.
7. Critical dimensions have been inspected after manufacture.
8. Functional testing confirms acceptable rigidity and fit.
9. Any significant issues have been documented during design review.
10. A final manufacturing-ready design has been released.